# Build artifacts
bin/
target/

# Cargo lock is committed for applications
# Cargo.lock

# Models (large files)
models/

# Local-only Cargo overrides. A `.cargo/config.toml` checked into
# the repo is legitimate (linker config, registry aliases, build
# flags shared across the team), but machine-specific environment
# overrides (e.g. `CUDA_COMPUTE_CAP`, `NVCC_CCBIN`, an SSH key path
# for a private registry) are per-developer and must not be
# committed. We block the common offender (`config.toml`) and leave
# the door open for project-level shared config in other files
# inside `.cargo/` — opt in with `git add -f` if a shared one is
# ever needed. See `CONTRIBUTING.md` "Building on hosts without
# CUDA / below candle's WMMA floor" for the full rationale and the
# one-liner that recreates the file locally on a Pascal laptop.
.cargo/config.toml

